  {
   "sectionTitle": "Customer Diversification",
   "layoutType": "two_column",
   "layoutData": {
    "left": {
     "title": "Diversified Revenue Base",
     "content": "Pacific Coast Logistics serves over 300 active customers across British Columbia and the Pacific Northwest, providing meaningful diversification while maintaining scale with anchor accounts.\n\nThe largest customer, Alderbrook Grocery Distributors, represents 22.0 percent of annual revenue under a master service agreement that runs through March 2027. The second-largest account, a building supply company, contributes approximately 8 percent, and no other single customer exceeds 7 percent of total volume.\n\nThe top six customers together account for just over half of annual revenue, and the remaining half is distributed across nearly 300 smaller accounts, including spot freight and seasonal shippers. The company has demonstrated its ability to retain major accounts for decades while continuously adding new customers through referrals and its reputation for reliability during supply chain disruptions.",
     "layoutType": "prose"
    },
    "right": {
     "title": "Revenue Concentration",
     "content": "\u2022 Total active customers: 300+\n\u2022 Largest customer (Alderbrook): 22.0%\n\u2022 Second-largest customer: ~8%\n\u2022 Top 5 customers: 47%\n\u2022 Top 10 customers: 63.5%\n\u2022 Food-related freight: ~50%\n\u2022 Remaining 290+ accounts: ~36.5%\n\nThe customer mix spans food distribution and grocery, building supply, beverage, pet food, furniture, and dairy sectors. Food-related freight represents approximately 50 percent of the business, reflecting the company's strength in temperature-controlled logistics and its long-standing relationships with grocery and produce distributors.\n\nThis diversification provides revenue stability while maintaining meaningful relationships with anchor accounts that have been with the company for over two decades.",
     "layoutType": "list"
    },
    "title": "Customer Diversification"
   }
  },
